W44-73: LZ77 + ANS in write_context_map_nonsimple (prerequisite for W44-71 / issue #59)
Date: 2026-05-19
Sibling workspace: ~/work/zen/jxl-encoder--w44-73-context-map-lz77
Commit: TBD (working on lynpprrx)

## Summary

W44-71 found the libjxl 15-cluster simple-default BlockCtxMap regresses bytes
because our `write_context_map_nonsimple` used Huffman+MTF only, while libjxl
uses ANS+LZ77 (`enc_context_map.cc:65-139` → `BuildAndEncodeHistograms` with
default HistogramParams: LZ77Method::kRLE + HybridUintMethod::kContextMap →
HybridUintConfig(2, 0, 1)).

This chunk ports the missing ANS+LZ77 path INTO our writer so the writer is
no longer the binding constraint. Cost-comparison gate picks the cheaper of
Huffman+MTF or ANS+LZ77 per call site.

## Implementation

- New `build_context_map_nonsimple_ans_lz77()` builds 1-context ANS code
  (or 2 contexts post-LZ77) over MTF-or-raw context-map tokens, applies
  RLE-LZ77 if outer num_contexts > 2 (libjxl's `decode_context_map` calls
  `Histograms::decode(1, br, allow_lz77 = num_contexts > 2)` — we must
  respect that gate or decoder errors `Lz77Disallowed`).
- Forces HybridUintConfig(2, 0, 1) per libjxl `enc_ans_params.h:81-90`
  `UintConfig()` when `uint_method == kContextMap`.
- Renamed old path to `write_context_map_nonsimple_huffman()` (Huffman+MTF).
- `write_context_map_nonsimple()` runs both, picks cheaper by raw bit count.
- Subtle: when post-LZ77 num_contexts == 1, the inner `decode_context_map`
  is SKIPPED by the decoder (`jxl-rs entropy_coding/decode.rs:576-634`,
  `libjxl dec_ans.cc:341-358`). My writer skips the 3-bit "simple,
  nbits=0" inner-context-map shortcut in that case to keep bit alignment.

## Acceptance gates

- (a) LZ77 path added to `write_context_map_nonsimple` — DONE
- (b) Cost-comparison gate — DONE (compares raw bit counts, picks cheaper)
- (c) 15-cluster test result — see below: NEGATIVE finding
- (d) Default behavior strictly better — DONE (every cell tested wins)
- (e) `cargo test --release` passes — DONE (1258 lib + 32 anim + 21 integration);
      1 PRE-EXISTING `test_animation_lossy_runs_cfl_pass_2` failure on baseline
      (delta 673 vs threshold 130 on bare main; W44-73 makes still smaller so
      delta=791 — both fail same gate, not introduced here).
- (f) djxl + jxl-rs + jxl-oxide roundtrip on flipped cells — DONE (18 checks)
- (g) Memory note + MEMORY.md entry — TODO
- (h) Hash-lock regen counted — 36 sidecars regenerated; net 4 noise/lz77
      tests SAVE 218 bytes each, rest byte-identical (hash differs in
      handful where path changed but bytes same).

## Acceptance gate (c) — NEGATIVE FINDING on 15-cluster

Applied W44-71 (15-cluster default) ON TOP of W44-73 and re-ran wedge cells:

Cell                       4c+W73    15c+W73   delta
1420710 e7 d=5.0           24589     24751     +162
1420710 e7 d=6.0           21212     21369     +157
1531677 e7 d=3.0           32022     32022     0
1531677 e7 d=5.0           21059     21270     +211
1531677 e7 d=6.0           18084     18346     +262
1189261 e7 d=3.0           30481     30481     0
1189261 e7 d=5.0           19778     19811     +33
1189261 e7 d=6.0           16816     17065     +249

15-cluster REGRESSES vs 4-cluster EVEN WITH the W73 writer. W44-69's
prediction that "cjxl's 7425 contexts cluster down tighter via pair-merge
than our 1980" doesn't pan out on these cells when measured through our
clustering / pair-merge path. cjxl must have additional levers (e.g.
different histogram pair-merge cost model, different ANS strategy) that
let it benefit from the finer-grained map. Honest-stop: W44-71 should NOT
be merged even after W73 lands.

## Baseline-vs-W73 measurements

19-cell paired sweep (6 CID22 photos x 4 distances, e7):
- Range: -0.05% to -2.30% per cell
- Average: -83.6 bytes per cell, -0.46% overall
- ALL cells win (zero regressions)

Screenshot cells (gb82-sc, 4 imgs x 3 distances, e7):
- Range: -0.08% to -0.46% per cell

Wedge cells from W44-69:
- 1420710 e7 d=6: 21295 → 21212 (-83B / -0.39%) vs cjxl 20653 (gap closed 14%)
- 1531677 e7 d=6: 18227 → 18084 (-143B / -0.78%)
- 1189261 e7 d=6: 16910 → 16816 (-94B / -0.56%)

## Decoder verification

All 18 paired decoder runs (3 images x 2 distances x 3 decoders) PASS:
djxl 0.12.0, jxl-rs (jxl_cli), jxl-oxide-imazen.

